Do not import eventlet in eventletutils until used

Seven oslo.messaging modules import eventletutils, which imports
eventlet. Find eventlet with importlib.util.find_spec() instead, and
import it when a function needs it: nothing can be monkey patched
before eventlet is imported. The public API behaves as before.

This saves nothing alone. With futurist's "Do not import eventlet until
it is needed" and oslo.messaging's "Find patched threading without
importing eventlet", glance-api's modules no longer load eventlet, and
their anonymous memory falls from 91MB to 82MB.

Prompt: Mikal asked for import-memory fixes that can be landed one at a
time and measured in devstack CI; eventletutils is one of the modules
that import eventlet in the threaded API services.

